Commands:
  cyberstrike completion            generate shell completion script
  cyberstrike acp                   start ACP (Agent Client Protocol) server
  cyberstrike mcp                   manage MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers
  cyberstrike [project]             start cyberstrike tui                                  [default]
  cyberstrike attach <url>          attach to a running cyberstrike server
  cyberstrike hackbrowser <target>  crawl a web app and open TUI for live analysis
  cyberstrike run [message..]       run cyberstrike with a message
  cyberstrike debug                 debugging and troubleshooting tools
  cyberstrike auth                  manage credentials
  cyberstrike agent                 manage agents
  cyberstrike upgrade [target]      upgrade cyberstrike to the latest or a specific version
                                                                                   [aliases: update]
  cyberstrike uninstall             uninstall cyberstrike and remove all related files
  cyberstrike serve                 starts a headless cyberstrike server
  cyberstrike web                   start cyberstrike server and open web interface
  cyberstrike models [provider]     list all available models
  cyberstrike stats                 show token usage and cost statistics
  cyberstrike export [sessionID]    export session data as JSON
  cyberstrike import <file>         import session data from JSON file or URL
  cyberstrike github                manage GitHub agent
  cyberstrike pr <number>           fetch and checkout a GitHub PR branch, then run cyberstrike
  cyberstrike session               manage sessions
  cyberstrike provider              manage local/custom AI providers
  cyberstrike skill                 manage offensive security skills

Positionals:
  project  path to start cyberstrike in                                                     [string]

Options:
  -h, --help         show help                                                             [boolean]
  -v, --version      show version number                                                   [boolean]
      --print-logs   print logs to stderr                                                  [boolean]
      --log-level    log level                  [string] [choices: "DEBUG", "INFO", "WARN", "ERROR"]
      --port         port to listen on                                      [number] [default: 4096]
      --hostname     hostname to listen on                           [string] [default: "127.0.0.1"]
      --mdns         enable mDNS service discovery (defaults hostname to 0.0.0.0)
                                                                          [boolean] [default: false]
      --mdns-domain  custom domain name for mDNS service (default: cyberstrike.local)
                                                             [string] [default: "cyberstrike.local"]
      --cors         additional domains to allow for CORS                      [array] [default: []]
  -m, --model        model to use in the format of provider/model                           [string]
  -c, --continue     continue the last session                                             [boolean]
  -s, --session      session id to continue                                                 [string]
      --fork         fork the session when continuing (use with --continue or --session)   [boolean]
      --prompt       prompt to use                                                          [string]
      --agent        agent to use                                                           [string]
